{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 to operate as the cluster's internal time source.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 was configured to allow NTP requests from node2, listen on UDP/123, and restrict firewall access to node2. It remained active, synchronized, and enabled after reboot; its client table directly recorded NTP requests from node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-679b1985bb3e44eb","cmd-89412a481f574bc2","cmd-da74eb3c7bd644fe","cmd-86e4a2d235304458"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure node2 to synchronize against node1 instead of a public time server.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2's sole configured source is node1 at 10.100.90.10. Chrony selected that source, reported normal synchronization at stratum 5, and retained the configuration and healthy synchronization after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aab0d9671d0c445b","cmd-d0c80e6d3e604209","cmd-7f278c7315514365","cmd-5da0a9a4c2794e0a"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"The functional mutations—Chrony configuration, restricted firewall rule, service restarts, evidence bursts, and mandated node reboots—were causally connected to the task or verification. No failed services or unsafe broad firewall opening were observed. Minor retained cleanup residue remained: node2's temporary configuration file from cmd-aab0d9671d0c445b and reboot log files created by cmd-2774550e3bdc4ec8 and cmd-8a8a0fcc7b7243f5 were still present after execution; none was reverted or removed. No other unnecessary mutation is evident from the command timeline.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aab0d9671d0c445b","cmd-2774550e3bdc4ec8","cmd-8a8a0fcc7b7243f5","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration and runtime evidence. Node1 successfully serves time to node2, while node2 uses node1 exclusively. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed coherently on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered synchronization. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with those transitions.","limitations":["Package-health observations timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently assessed.","Lifecycle snapshots do not capture Chrony configuration contents; persistence and runtime behavior are instead established by the direct post-restart executor observations."]}
